# Boot 6.12 over JTAG when a Pluto is plugged in.
#
# NO serial condition here, deliberately. udev fails ANY ATTR test -- == or !=
# -- when the attribute does not exist, and on 5.10 the USB serial attribute is
# absent from sysfs entirely. So "ATTR{serial}!=\"?*\"" never matches either, and
# there is no udev-level way to say "serial is absent".
#
# The loop guard therefore lives in the script: a board already running 6.12
# DOES report a serial (derived from the SPI-NOR UniqueID), so it skips. Without
# that check a successful boot re-enumerates and retriggers this forever.
#
# RUN+= must return promptly -- udev kills the process group when the handler
# returns -- so the work is handed to a systemd unit.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0456", ATTR{idProduct}=="b673", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="pluto-autoboot612.service"
